\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Project: RHS Course Recommendation API
\f1\b0  \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 What the system does
\f1\b0 \
This is a backend REST API that takes a student's transcript and academic profile as input and returns a personalized, prerequisite-validated course plan as output. It is written in Python and follows a three-layer architecture: data \uc0\u8594  logic \u8594  API.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 File by file
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs26 \cf0 RHS_POS_2026-2027_rules.json
\f1\b0\fs24  This is the knowledge base. It encodes all 119 courses from Ridge High School's official Program of Studies as structured JSON. Each course entry contains its department, credit value, eligible grade levels, and a prerequisite tree expressed as a recursive logical structure using 
\f3\fs26 all_of
\f1\fs24  / 
\f3\fs26 any_of
\f1\fs24  / 
\f3\fs26 min_grade
\f1\fs24  / 
\f3\fs26 completed_group
\f1\fs24  nodes. It also encodes scheduling policy \'97 AP limits by grade, study hall triggers, graduation requirements, and biannual course availability. Everything the system knows about RHS rules lives here.\

\f2\b\fs26 rhs_rules_schema.json
\f1\b0\fs24  A JSON Schema (Draft-07) that validates the rules file. It defines the allowed structure for every field and every prerequisite node type. Running a validator against this schema catches data entry errors \'97 for example, a missing required field or an invalid prerequisite type \'97 before they cause silent bugs in the logic layer.\

\f2\b\fs26 evaluator.py
\f1\b0\fs24  The core logic engine. It exposes one main public function: 
\f3\fs26 evaluate(rules, transcript, course_code, student_grade)
\f1\fs24 . Internally it wraps the student's transcript in a 
\f3\fs26 Transcript
\f1\fs24  class that supports lookups like "what is the best grade the student earned in any course from the biology group." It then walks the prerequisite tree recursively \'97 evaluating each node type and propagating pass/fail results upward. It handles hard gates (grade thresholds, grade level restrictions) separately from soft gates (concurrent enrollment requirements, which are collected as warnings rather than blockers). It returns a structured dict indicating eligibility, blocking reasons, corequisite requirements, and scheduling constraints.\

\f2\b\fs26 recommender.py
\f1\b0\fs24  Sits on top of the evaluator. Its main function 
\f3\fs26 build_slate()
\f1\fs24  iterates over all courses in the rules file, calls 
\f3\fs26 evaluate()
\f1\fs24  for each one, scores eligible courses using a weighted formula (base score by level + career track bonus + college tier multiplier), and groups them by schedule slot (English, Math, Science, etc.). A second function 
\f3\fs26 build_two_year_plan()
\f1\fs24  simulates completing Year 1 at a B+ grade and runs the same process for Year 2, giving a two-year forward projection. All weights and bonuses are externalized to the config file so they can be tuned without touching code.\

\f2\b\fs26 recommender_config.json
\f1\b0\fs24  External configuration for the recommender. Contains career track bonus scores (e.g., AP Economics gets +55 points for a Business/Finance student), college tier multipliers, and gate type classifications. Separating this from the Python code means a counselor or administrator can adjust recommendation weights without needing to edit or redeploy code.\

\f2\b\fs26 recommender_api.py
\f1\b0\fs24  A FastAPI web server that wraps the evaluator and recommender as HTTP endpoints. FastAPI is a modern Python framework that auto-generates an interactive docs page (
\f3\fs26 /docs
\f1\fs24 ) and handles request validation via Pydantic models. The API accepts POST requests with a student profile as JSON and returns the course plan as JSON. This is what a front-end application would call.\

\f2\b\fs26 requirements.txt
\f1\b0\fs24  Lists all third-party Python packages the project depends on \'97 FastAPI, Uvicorn (the ASGI web server), and Pydantic.\

\f2\b\fs26 .env
\f1\b0\fs24  Stores environment variables locally \'97 specifically the file paths for the rules JSON and config JSON. This means the same code can run in different environments (your laptop, a school server, a cloud host) just by changing the 
\f3\fs26 .env
\f1\fs24  file rather than editing source code.\

\f2\b\fs26 .gitignore
\f1\b0\fs24  Tells Git which files to exclude from version control \'97 the virtual environment folder, 
\f3\fs26 __pycache__
\f1\fs24 , and the 
\f3\fs26 .env
\f1\fs24  file (since it may contain sensitive local paths).\

\f2\b\fs26 .vscode/settings.json
\f1\b0\fs24  VS Code workspace configuration. It points the Python interpreter to the local virtual environment, enables format-on-save, and injects the 
\f3\fs26 .env
\f1\fs24  variables automatically into every VS Code terminal session so you don't have to set them manually each time.\
